 "text": "You don't need more willpower to stop checking your phone, you need distance. Every time it buzzes, picking it up takes one second, and one second is all your brain needs to say yes. So make it harder, put the phone in another room, close the door and start a 25-minute timer on your laptop. Now checking it means standing up and walking to the door, that little pause is usually enough to keep you working. Say you're studying for an exam, one block 20 pages, a second block 20 more, phone in the kitchen both times. When the timer ends, take a 5-minute break, check whatever you want, then go again. Pick the room right now, tomorrow your first block starts with the phone in the kitchen. That's what Demure is for, you archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.",
